S=[]
S.append(("Huntsville at a glance","""<p>Huntsville is the county seat of Madison County, and its population is 233,627, the largest of any city in Alabama. The city limits also reach into Limestone, Morgan and Marshall counties, so two houses with a Huntsville mailing address can sit in different tax jurisdictions. Check the parcel record before you assume anything about your bill. The Madison County Tax Collector only bills property that lies in Madison County.</p><p>Aerospace and defense work drive local demand. Redstone Arsenal, Cummings Research Park and NASA's Marshall center are the big hubs, and a household that relocates for a contract or a plant job often has to sell on a deadline. A flexible closing date can matter as much as the price.</p><p>Housing stock runs from Old Town homes built in the late 1820s to the ranch houses and split levels that spread out after Redstone Arsenal became a rocket research center. Many of the postwar houses now need roofs, wiring and plumbing. A house inside a historic district can carry design review rules, so ask the city before you plan exterior work or demolition.</p>"""))
S.append(("Due dates and payment options","""<p>The Madison County Tax Collector bills and collects property tax for houses in the Madison County part of Huntsville. Taxes are due October 1 and become delinquent after December 31. A bill covers the period from the previous October 1 through September 30 of the current year.</p><p>Alabama law does not require a bill before taxes turn delinquent. The office mails a courtesy notice by October 1 and a final notice after January 1, but if nothing arrives you still owe the tax. Call 256-532-3370 or look the parcel up online.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Payment method</th><th>Cost or limit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Card or debit</td><td>2.75 percent convenience fee plus $0.30</td></tr><tr><td>E-check</td><td>$1.50</td></tr><tr><td>Real property in April and May</td><td>Certified funds, cash or cards only</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The main office is in the Madison County Service Center, 1918 Memorial Parkway NW, Huntsville, open Monday to Friday, 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. A satellite office sits at 100 Plaza Blvd. in Madison.</p>"""))
S.append(("Tax rate and how the bill is built","""<p>The county lists $5.80 per $100 of assessed value for property inside the Huntsville city limits. Madison is listed at $6.95, Triana at $6.15, and New Hope, Gurley and Owens Cross Roads at $4.05. Unincorporated land is listed at $3.35 and improvements at $3.65.</p><p>Assessed value starts with the appraised value times the class percentage. Alabama sets 30 percent for utilities, 20 percent for other property, and 10 percent for agricultural land, timber and owner-occupied single-family homes. The county's regular homestead worksheet then deducts $48 when assessed value is $4,000 or more.</p><p>Your real bill depends on your own appraisal and exemptions, so pull the parcel record and read the figures that apply to your house.</p>"""))
S.append(("What happens if the tax goes unpaid?","""<p>A $5.00 late fee applies after December 31, and interest runs at 1 percent per month on the base amount. Probate and advertising fees get added too.</p><p>The state timetable starts with delinquency on January 1. The case moves to the probate court in February, the probate court meets in March, advertising runs in April and a tax sale follows in May. Madison County holds its annual lien sale online in May.</p><p>Paying before the sale costs far less than paying after it. If back taxes are the reason you want out of the house, tell the buyer and the title company early so the payoff figure goes on the settlement statement.</p>"""))
S.append(("How to appeal your assessment","""<p>File a written protest with the Madison County Board of Equalization on the second floor of the Madison County Service Center, 1918 Memorial Parkway NW. The county cites Code of Alabama sections 40-3-20, 40-3-24 and 40-3-25.</p><ul><li>New values usually post in March or April, announced by newspaper ad two weeks in a row.</li><li>You have 30 days from the second ad to appeal.</li><li>A county appraiser reviews the case first, then a hearing is set if you still disagree.</li><li>A circuit court appeal must be filed within 30 days after the board adjourns, and the tax must be paid by December 31 or a bond posted for double the tax.</li></ul><p>Bring photos of any damage, repair estimates and recent sales of similar houses nearby. Those are the things an appraiser can actually weigh.</p>"""))
S.append(("What happens to the tax bill when you sell?","""<p>The bill follows the owner of record on October 1 of the previous year, so a buyer can receive a notice in the seller's name. New owners should confirm the deed is recorded in the probate office at the Madison County Service Center, then assess the property in the Tax Assessor's Office and claim exemptions.</p><p>A title company normally prorates the year's tax between buyer and seller at closing. Ask for the proration worksheet and keep your copy of the paid receipt. If the tax is still owed, the title company requests the payoff figure from the tax collector and pays it from your proceeds at closing.</p>"""))
S.append(("Ground and weather problems that surface at sale","""<p>Storms are the main risk here. Spring and late fall bring large hail, straight-line wind and tornadoes, and the city sits in the area called Dixie Alley, where long-track tornadoes are more common than in most of the country. Hail and wind damage show up as roof and siding problems, and buyers who need financing or insurance will ask about them.</p><p>The land under the city is karst, with caves through the limestone bedrock. That can mean sinkholes and drainage surprises. Settling cracks, sticking doors or a soft spot in the yard will draw attention from a retail buyer's inspector.</p><p>A cash buyer who accepts the house as it stands avoids that back and forth.</p>"""))
S.append(("Common situations for Huntsville sellers","""<ul><li>Inherited houses with several heirs and no clear owner of record.</li><li>Older mill-village and Old Town houses that need major systems work.</li><li>Hail-damaged roofs from spring storms.</li><li>Job moves tied to Redstone Arsenal, Cummings Research Park or the auto plants.</li><li>Delinquent tax on a rental or vacant house.</li></ul><p>Each of these is easier with a buyer who closes on your schedule and takes the house in its current condition. Cash Home Buyers makes written offers on Huntsville houses and works with a local title company to clear unpaid tax from the proceeds. A cash sale skips the lender appraisal, the repair negotiation and the financing contingency, which are the usual places a sale stalls.</p>"""))
F=[("What is the Huntsville property tax rate?","The county lists $5.80 per $100 of assessed value inside the Huntsville city limits. Property in the Limestone, Morgan or Marshall portions of the city is billed by those counties, so check your parcel."),
("When is Huntsville property tax due?","Taxes are due October 1 and become delinquent after December 31. The county mails a courtesy notice by October 1 but does not have to."),
("Where do I pay property tax in Huntsville?","Pay the Madison County Tax Collector at the Madison County Service Center, 1918 Memorial Parkway NW, or at the satellite office at 100 Plaza Blvd. in Madison. You can also pay online or by mail, and the main office number is 256-532-3370."),
("What is the penalty for late property tax in Huntsville?","A $5.00 late fee applies after December 31, plus 1 percent interest per month on the base amount and added probate and advertising costs. Unpaid parcels can go to the May online lien sale."),
("Can I sell a Huntsville house that owes back taxes?","Yes. The unpaid tax is paid from the sale proceeds at closing, and the title company will request the payoff figure from the tax collector.")]
w('huntsville-al-property-tax-guide',S,F)
